只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"OpenBKN's DeepSeek Harness Web UI plugin enables business users to safely, accurately and reliably utilize the enterprise's business knowledge network to complete business analysis and decision-making.","id":"gh:1356577235","install_available":false,"language":"TypeScript","name":"bkn-dsh","slug":"openbkn-ai/bkn-dsh","topics":["dsh-plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"OpenBKN's DeepSeek Harness Web UI plugin enables business users to safely, accurately and reliably u"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"tilize the enterprise's business knowledge network to complete business analysis and decision-making"},{"id":"p1s3","text":"ilize the enterprise's business knowledge network to complete business analysis and decision-making."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# bkn-dsh"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"> Revision `0.2.1-rc.3-openbkn.0.2.1-3` admits DSH `0.2.1-rc.3` and every newer version, including a"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"lpha, rc, stable and future major releases; `0.2.0-rc.2` remains admitted. Loading admission is dist"},{"id":"p3s3","text":"inct from verified compatibility. Build/test anchors remain pinned, and existing interface, permissi"},{"id":"p3s4","text":"on and dependency-identity checks remain enabled."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Release target: `0.2.1-rc.3-openbkn.0.2.1-3`, retaining the exact accepted CI6 archive. Publication "},{"id":"p4s2","text":"is complete only after the matching npm version and GitHub Release exist. See the formal acceptance "},{"id":"p4s3","text":"record. See the plugin instructions for automatic login, packaged MCP and trust boundaries; developm"},{"id":"p4s4","text":"ent records below retain their historical verdicts."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"**Recent updates (September 21–October 12):** English · 中文."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"**Illustrated user guide:** English · 中文 · PDF (中文). Includes installation, CLI setup, sign-in, supp"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"ly-chain Q&A;, provenance, and diagnostics with numbered screenshots."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Published -7 history: GitHub Release, cumulative update notes, and publication verification. Histori"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"cal -5/-6 packages and earlier -7 candidates retain their original identities; acceptance remains li"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"mited to the recorded artifacts and scenarios."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"中文"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"Bring governed OpenBKN business knowledge into DeepSeek Harness conversations."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## 0.2.1 version and compatibility"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"This revision adds a fixed official CLI `0.2.1` installation target while retaining `0.1.5`/`0.2.0`,"},{"id":"p11s2","text":" explicit selection and existing-installation protection. Use the CLI matching the platform: CLI `0."},{"id":"p11s3","text":"2.0` rejects a fresh login against platform `0.2.1`. The final increment uses formal OpenBKN `0.2.1`"},{"id":"p11s4","text":" CE and CLI `0.2.1`; prior formal `0.2.0` and Enterprise provenance evidence remains separately attr"},{"id":"p11s5","text":"ibuted. See the formal acceptance record for artifact identity, actual coverage and limitations."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Loading admission remains `0.2.0-rc.2 || >=0.2.1-rc.3`, without an upper bound. Native affected-path"},{"id":"p12s2","text":" acceptance uses official Desktop `0.2.1-rc.5` on Mac and Windows; admission does not claim verified"},{"id":"p12s3","text":" compatibility with every newer release. Community deployments do not supply Enterprise provenance r"},{"id":"p12s4","text":"outes. Published content, invalid/unknown states and model answers remain platform-owned."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"This revision ships the native MCP same-origin protection with the plugin and loads it through the b"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"usiness module; no separate profile companion or official Host modification is required. Companion i"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"nstructions for the earlier base release remain historical. Frozen -30/-31/-32 and historical verdic"},{"id":"p13s4","text":"he earlier base release remain historical. Frozen -30/-31/-32 and historical verdicts are preserved."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"### Historical development checkpoints"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"## Why"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"Enterprise decisions need trusted business objects, metrics, rules, relationships, and permission-aw"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"are evidence. General-purpose chat alone does not provide that governed context."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"## What"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"bkn-dsh is an additive DeepSeek Harness plugin that lets authorized users select one OpenBKN busines"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"s knowledge network for a conversation, analyze within that explicit scope, and inspect available bu"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"siness provenance for each completed answer."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"## Who it serves"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"- Business users and analysts who need explainable, governed analysis.\n- Knowledge-network owners wh"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"o want their business semantics reused consistently.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"### Backup and known limitations"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"- **Backup and moving machines**: copy `$DSH_HOME/openbkn/session-bindings/` (per-session network bi"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"ndings) and `$DSH_HOME/storages/openbkn_workspace_bindings.json` (workspace ↔ network associations) "},{"id":"p24s3","text":"together with the session logs. Provenance and conversation continuity are re-derived from the sessi"},{"id":"p24s4","text":"on log, but the bindings are not.\n- **Network scope — important limitation of the platform `run_code"},{"id":"p24s5","text":"`**: in a bound session the plugin refuses any direct query whose `kn_id` is missing or names anothe"},{"id":"p24s6","text":"r network, and it does not offer action execution. But the platform's `run_code`, `execute_skill` wh"},{"id":"p24s7","text":"ere the deployment enables it (and `execute_published_tool`) run on the platform: from OpenBKN 0.1.5"},{"id":"p24s8","text":" on, a `run_code` script can call every other platform tool as a function — including other networks"},{"id":"p24s9","text":"' queries and `execute_action` — and models often prefer it. Calls made inside the script do not pas"},{"id":"p24s10","text":"s through the plugin, so there the bound network and the no-action rule rest on the session prompt o"},{"id":"p24s11","text":"nly. Every platform operation still appears with its receipt in the business provenance. Platform-si"},{"id":"p24s12","text":"de scoping of `run_code` is being worked out with the OpenBKN team.\n- **Unbound sessions**: OpenBKN "},{"id":"p24s13","text":"tools are refused in any session that is not bound through the OpenBKN panel, including a session wh"},{"id":"p24s14","text":"ose binding record cannot be read, or conflicts with its log, when the session is opened. Such a ses"},{"id":"p24s15","text":"sion still opens and keeps its history; the plugin logs a payload-free warning, but the UI does not "},{"id":"p24s16","text":"show a binding-error state yet. A record that becomes unreadable while its session is already runnin"},{"id":"p24s17","text":"g does not revoke the running session's access until the session is reopened.\n- **Associations are s"},{"id":"p24s18","text":"hared by every host and profile** in one `$DSH_HOME` (`storages/openbkn_workspace_bindings.json`): a"},{"id":"p24s19","text":" network associated in `dsh web` offers *continue* / *new session* in the desktop app, not *New work"},{"id":"p24s20","text":"ted in `dsh web` offers *continue* / *new session* in the desktop app, not *New workspace*.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"## Prerequisites and trial path"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"The plugin needs a reachable OpenBKN platform with at least one knowledge network you can access."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"1. **Platform** — run one locally with bkn-foundry (`deploy/dev/mac.sh` on macOS; Docker engine with"},{"id":"p27s2","text":" ≥16 GB memory), or use your organization's deployment.\n2. **Sample data** — import a sample knowled"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"ge network from bkn-samples (`supply_ontology_hand` is the primary end-to-end dataset).\n3. **Configu"},{"id":"p27s4","text":"re and authorize** — enter the platform address in the OpenBKN panel, then use its CLI sign-in actio"},{"id":"p27s5","text":"n. The plugin reads the token through the CLI handshake only.\n4. **Bind** — open the OpenBKN panel i"},{"id":"p27s6","text":"n DSH, pick the network, and start a session in its workspace."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
